# ReportGen — Complete Database Flow & Optimization Analysis
> **Scope:** Every MongoDB collection, every read/write pattern, every data journey, every bottleneck.
> **Based on:** Full source read of all 18 models + routes + utils + flow diagram.
> **Created:** 2026-04-29

---

## Part 1 — The 18 Collections at a Glance

| # | Collection | Purpose | Who Creates | Approval? |
|---|-----------|---------|------------|-----------|
| 1 | `users` | All accounts (student + admin) | Registration | No |
| 2 | `degrees` | B.Tech, BCA, MBA, etc. | Admin only | No |
| 3 | `departments` | Sub-groups within a Degree | Admin or Student | Yes (student) |
| 4 | `majors` | Specialization + AI config hub | Admin only | No |
| 5 | `universities` | Institution master records | Admin or Student | Yes (student) |
| 6 | `colleges` | College under a University | Admin or Student | Yes (student) |
| 7 | `industries` | Internship company records | Admin or Student | Yes (student) |
| 8 | `reports` | The core report document | Student | No |
| 9 | `payments` | Payment transaction records | System | No |
| 10 | `services` | Pricing + product definitions | Admin | No |
| 11 | `internshiptypes` | **LEGACY** internship categories | Admin | No |
| 12 | `project_titles` | Suggested titles per Major | Admin | No |
| 13 | `work_keywords` | Tag library for brief description | Admin | No |
| 14 | `university_report_templates` | Section config for university | Admin | No |
| 15 | `college_report_templates` | Section config for college | Admin | No |
| 16 | `major_report_templates` | Section config for major | Admin | No |
| 17 | `audit_logs` | Admin action trail | System | No |
| 18 | `report_content_types` | Content type labels | Admin | No |

---

## Part 2 — Full Data Flow Per User Journey

### Journey 1: Student Registration → Profile Completion

```
WRITE: users (create) → email, password(bcrypt), role='student', profileCompleted=False

PUT /api/student/profile/personal
  WRITE: users.name, villageCityName, tehsil, district, state, phone, gender

PUT /api/student/profile/college
  READ:  universities (filter approvalStatus='approved' OR createdBy=me)
  READ:  colleges (filter university=selected, approvalStatus='approved' OR createdBy=me)
  READ:  degrees (filter isActive=True)
  READ:  departments (filter degree=selected, approvalStatus='approved')
  READ:  majors (filter degree=selected, isActive=True)
  WRITE: users.university, college, degree, academicDepartment, major,
         rollNumber, enrollmentNumber, semester

PUT /api/student/profile/industry
  READ:  industries (filter approvalStatus='approved' OR createdBy=me)
  WRITE: users.industry, supervisorName, supervisorContact
  WRITE: users.industryProfileCustomized=True/False
  WRITE: users.industryVillageCityName, industryType, industrySubType,
         industryKeyActivities, industryDetails, industryWebsite, industryGstNumber

  [PROFILE COMPLETE CHECK]
  READ:  users.university, college, degree, major, industry  ← all must be non-null
  WRITE: users.profileCompleted = True
```

**Data Shape Note:** The `User` document is a **fat document**. It holds a full snapshot of the student's industry data (11 fields) alongside all academic references. This is intentional — student overrides must never mutate the master `Industry` record.

---

### Journey 2: Admin Creates Academic Hierarchy

```
POST /admin/degrees
  WRITE: degrees {name, isActive}

POST /admin/departments
  WRITE: departments {name, degree(ref), approvalStatus='approved', createdBy}

POST /admin/majors
  WRITE: majors {
    name, degree(ref), department(ref, optional),
    reportLanguage, reportContentType,   ← stored as plain STRING (weakness)
    aiPromptContext,
    reportPolicy: {
      strictLanguageOnly, allowedLanguages,
      generationInstruction, uiLabels(dict),
      sectionTitleMap(dict), contentFeatures(list),
      imagesRequired
    },
    reportSections: [                     ← LEGACY embedded list
      {key, title, description}
    ],
    employmentOpportunities: [{companyType, positions}]
  }

POST /admin/universities
  WRITE: universities {name, city, district, state, website, logo, approvalStatus='approved'}

POST /admin/colleges
  READ:  universities
  WRITE: colleges {name, university(ref), city, ..., approvalStatus='approved'}
```

---

### Journey 3: Admin Configures Report Section Templates (The 3-Level Cascade)

```
POST /admin/report-sections/university
  READ:  universities
  WRITE: university_report_templates {
    university(ref, UNIQUE), sections[{key, title, description, sortOrder}],
    isActive, description, createdBy
  }

POST /admin/report-sections/college
  READ:  universities → colleges
  WRITE: college_report_templates {
    college(ref, UNIQUE), university(ref),   ← university denormalized for filtering
    sections[{...}],
    useUniversityDefault=True/False,         ← True = ignore own sections, inherit up
    isActive, createdBy
  }

POST /admin/report-sections/major
  READ:  universities → colleges → majors
  WRITE: major_report_templates {
    major(ref, UNIQUE), college(ref), university(ref),   ← both denormalized
    sections[{...}],
    useLevelAboveDefault=True/False,         ← True = ignore own sections, inherit up
    isActive, createdBy
  }
```

**The Cascade Resolver (`utils/report_sections.py`) at runtime:**

```
resolve_effective_report_sections(major, college, university):
  1. MajorReportTemplate.objects(major=major_id).first()
     → if exists AND useLevelAboveDefault=False AND sections not empty
     → RETURN source='major_custom'                          [1 DB query]

  2. CollegeReportTemplate.objects(college=college_id).first()
     → if exists AND useUniversityDefault=False AND sections not empty
     → RETURN source='college_custom'                        [1 DB query]

  3. UniversityReportTemplate.objects(university=university_id).first()
     → if exists AND sections not empty
     → RETURN source='university_default'                    [1 DB query]

  4. major_doc.reportSections (embedded in Major)
     → if not empty
     → RETURN source='major_legacy'                          [0 extra DB queries]

  5. RETURN source='none' → n8n uses hardcoded defaults
```

**Total DB hits for section resolution: 3 queries maximum** — already efficient. However, each query is a `.first()` with no field projection, fetching the entire template document including the sections array.

---

### Journey 4: Student Creates a Report

```
GET /student/create-report
  READ: users.major → major doc (reportLanguage, reportContentType, reportPolicy)
  READ: project_titles (filter major=user.major) → suggested titles
  READ: work_keywords (filter industryType=user.industryType, jobProfile=user.jobProfile)
        ← PROBLEM: text-match filter only, no FK to major

POST /api/reports/
  INPUT: {majorId, projectTitle, workKeywords[], briefDescription, ...}

  READ:  users (current) — full profile with all refs
  READ:  majors (major_id)
  READ:  industries (user.industry)
  READ:  colleges (user.college)
  READ:  universities (user.university)
  READ:  degrees (user.degree)

  WRITE: reports {
    user(ref), degree(ref), major(ref), college(ref), university(ref),
    industry(ref),
    projectTitle, internshipTitle, academicYear,
    rollNumber, studentEmail,
    supervisorName, supervisorContact,
    duration, startDate, endDate, positionTitle,
    briefDescription, keySkills,
    reportLanguage,
    status='generating',
    generatedContent={}, editedContent={},
    sectionImages={},
    isPaid=False,
    createdAt, updatedAt
  }

  CALL: resolve_effective_report_sections(major, college, university)
        → 1–3 DB queries (template cascade)

  BUILD: full n8n payload (in memory, no more DB hits)
  POST:  n8n webhook (HTTP, synchronous, timeout=120s)
```

**Report creation DB reads:** 6 separate document fetches (user, major, industry, college, university, degree). These are all single-document lookups by `_id`.

---

### Journey 5: n8n Callback → Report Saved

```
PUT /api/reports/{id}/generated    ← called by n8n, not by student
  READ:  reports (find by id)
  WRITE: reports.generatedContent = {
    "acknowledgement": "...",
    "abstract": "...",
    "workDescription": "...",
    ... (one key per section)
  }
  WRITE: reports.generatedTitles = {"sectionKey": "Displayed Title", ...}
  WRITE: reports.generatedUiLabels = {"label key": "value", ...}
  WRITE: reports.status = 'generated'
  WRITE: reports.updatedAt
```

**The `generatedContent` DictField** stores the entire AI-generated report as a single embedded JSON blob. Sections are keys, content is values. This is the **most read-heavy field** in the system.

---

### Journey 6: Student Edits & Downloads PDF

```
GET /api/reports/{id}
  READ: reports (by id)
  READ: users (report.user)
  READ: major, college, university, degree, industry  ← if not already cached
  → Returns full report JSON to browser

PUT /api/reports/{id}/content
  WRITE: reports.editedContent = {
    "sectionKey": "student-edited text",
    "__cover": { logos: [...], ... },
    "__coverPage": { ... },
    "__layout": { header, footer, ... }
  }
  WRITE: reports.status = 'edited'

POST /api/reports/{id}/images/{section}
  WRITE: reports.sectionImages[section] = [
    {url, filename, position, caption, widthPercent}
  ]

GET /api/reports/{id}/pdf
  READ: reports (by id, full document)
  READ: users (report.user)
  READ: major.reportPolicy (for sectionTitleMap, uiLabels)
  BUILD: _build_pdf_sections() → merges generatedContent + editedContent
  RENDER: pdf_template.html via Playwright → PDF bytes
  WRITE: reports.downloadCount += 1
  RETURN: application/pdf
```

---

### Journey 7: Payment Flow (Planned, Partially Implemented)

```
GET /api/services (type='report')
  READ: services {name, price, gstPercent, freeLimit, degreePricing[{degree(ref), price}]}

POST /api/payments/
  READ: services
  READ: users (check report count vs freeLimit) ← NOT IMPLEMENTED YET
  WRITE: payments {
    user(ref), service(DynamicField!), report(ref),
    amount, gstAmount, totalAmount,
    status='pending', paymentMethod, transactionId
  }

[After gateway callback]
  WRITE: payments.status = 'completed'
  WRITE: reports.isPaid = True
  WRITE: reports.payment = payment_ref
```

**CRITICAL BUG:** `Payment.service` is declared as `DynamicField` (not `ReferenceField('Service')`). This means no referential integrity — if a Service is renamed or deleted, old payment records have orphaned/incorrect data.

---

### Journey 8: Student Submits New Entity (Approval Workflow)

```
POST /api/student/universities/  (or /colleges/, /industries/, /departments/)
  WRITE: universities {
    name, city, ...,
    approvalStatus='pending',
    createdBy=user_ref
  }

  [Student sees it immediately via visibility rule:]
  READ filter: (approvalStatus='approved') OR (createdBy=current_user.id)

Admin Panel:
  READ: universities (filter approvalStatus='pending')
  WRITE: universities.approvalStatus = 'approved' OR 'rejected'
  WRITE: universities.rejectionReason = '...'   ← set on rejection
  WRITE: audit_logs {user(admin_ref), action, targetType, targetId, timestamp}
```

