## Part 4 — Query Performance Analysis

### Current Index Coverage

| Collection | Indexed Fields | Status |
|-----------|---------------|--------|
| `users` | `email` (unique) | ✅ Good |
| `majors` | `(degree, name)` unique compound | ✅ Good |
| `university_report_templates` | `university` unique | ✅ Good |
| `college_report_templates` | `college` unique | ✅ Good |
| `major_report_templates` | `major` unique | ✅ Good |
| `degrees` | `name` unique | ✅ Good |
| `reports` | **NONE defined** | 🔴 Missing |
| `industries` | **NONE defined** | 🔴 Missing |
| `universities` | **NONE defined** | 🔴 Missing |
| `colleges` | **NONE defined** | 🔴 Missing |
| `work_keywords` | **NONE defined** | 🔴 Missing |
| `project_titles` | **NONE defined** | 🔴 Missing |
| `payments` | **NONE defined** | 🔴 Missing |
| `audit_logs` | **NONE defined** | 🔴 Missing |

### Most Frequent Queries (Hot Paths)

```python
# 1. Every page load for a logged-in student:
User.objects(id=session_user_id).first()            # ← hits email index ✅

# 2. Create Report page — work keyword load:
WorkKeyword.objects(industryType=x, jobProfile=y)  # ← full collection scan 🔴

# 3. Admin dashboard — pending approvals:
University.objects(approvalStatus='pending')        # ← full collection scan 🔴
College.objects(approvalStatus='pending')           # ← full collection scan 🔴
Industry.objects(approvalStatus='pending')          # ← full collection scan 🔴

# 4. Student report list:
Report.objects(user=user_id).order_by('-createdAt') # ← full scan 🔴

# 5. College dropdown in profile:
College.objects(university=uni_id, approvalStatus='approved')  # ← full scan 🔴

# 6. Section cascade resolver:
MajorReportTemplate.objects(major=major_id).first() # ← hits unique index ✅
CollegeReportTemplate.objects(college=cid).first()  # ← hits unique index ✅
UniversityReportTemplate.objects(university=uid).first() # ← hits unique index ✅
```

